{"availability":"available","full":"ryanbrunner/gloss","name":"gloss","description":"Explore this public GitHub project.","category":"Other","language":"TypeScript","stars":1,"forks":0,"created":"2026-09-28T12:47:32Z","updated":"2026-10-02T01:48:01Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":null,"topics":[],"demo":null,"color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-03T08:24:09.857Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-03T08:24:09.857Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-03T08:24:09.857Z","lastDemoCheckedAt":"2026-10-03T08:24:09.857Z","discoveredVia":[],"metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-03T08:24:09.857Z","stars":1,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Review a running web app in a browser with a feedback bar across the top, and hand what you wrote to Claude.","gloss open opens the page in a Chromium window with the Gloss bar over it. The reviewer writes comments in the bar and presses Submit to send them to Claude as a round. Claude applies them and the window reloads with its summary of what changed. This repeats until the reviewer presses Approve.","Gloss never fixes anything itself. It is the channel between the reviewer and whatever runs Claude (Claude Code, or Reeve). The agent drives the session with four short commands: gloss wait for the reviewer's verdict, gloss working and gloss ready either side of its changes, and gloss close. The Claude Code plugin in this repo runs that loop for you."],"features":["The page is untouched. It loads from its real origin. A proxy would","A strict CSP doesn't stop it. Init scripts run whatever the page's CSP","It follows you. New tabs, client-side navigation and full reloads all","HTTPS dev hosts load, with ignoreHTTPSErrors, as in Reeve's screenshots."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/ryanbrunner/gloss/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"5b0c7e2e662f645b8bd27ec3e7c5ada8ca04154b19ddee8148a8f89def5cace6","extractedAt":"2026-10-03T08:24:09.857Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-03T14:17:53.471Z",